elgium\\nUZ Leuven, Belgium\\n“EHA offers the potential to be part of a community that is broader than a national society, which offers great opportunities to meet colleagues from different countries at events like the Congress.”\\nProf Anne Angelillo-Scherrer, Community Stakeholder Committee Member\\nUniversity of Bern, Switzerland\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-6f5b02f93bee7af3c5bb4d0c\", \"title\": \"Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3994, \"end\": 4038, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 44}, {\"start\": 4135, \"end\": 4192, \"excerpt_start\": 45, \"excerpt_end\": 102}, {\"start\": 4305, \"end\": 5804, \"excerpt_start\": 103, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\\nLeft Sidebar\\n2 min read · May 16, 2025\\nMay 16, 2025\\nShare\\nWhat is precision hematology?\\nPrecision hematology is an integrated approach to diagnosing and treating blood disorders—particularly hematologic malignancies—by leveraging detailed molecular, genetic, and functional information about each patient’s disease.\\nIt matches therapies more precisely to individual patients by uniting innovative clinical trial designs with cutting-edge diagnostics, such as:\\nAdvanced imaging\\nGenetic profiling\\nDrug-sensitivity testing\\nThis field brings together physicians, scientists, and other key stakeholders across preclinical, translational, and clinical research. Through this collaboration, precision hematology aims to:\\nAccelerate the discovery of new treatment strategies\\nRefine therapeutic decision-making\\nImprove outcomes for patients with blood cancers\\nOur program’s goals\\nOur Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program is designed to promote innovative concepts for diagnostics and innovative clinical trial designs which will feed into the clinical application of precision hematology.\\nThe goal of the program is to create a European regulatory framework for precision hematology. By increasing awareness and providing education, guidelines, and policies, we can improve access to:\\nDiagnostics\\nClinical research\\nTreatment in malignant hematology\\nUseful materials\\nEHA Position Paper on Personalized Treatment for Hematologic Diseases\\nPrecision Medicine in Hematology in 2021: Definitions, Tools, Perspectives, and Open Questions\\nIn Vitro Diagnostic Medical\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-4a63fc37665d223b724eb647\", \"title\": \"Research & Innovation - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Research & Innovation - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3902, \"end\": 4532, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 630}, {\"start\": 4773, \"end\": 4793, \"excerpt_start\": 631, \"excerpt_end\": 651}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Research & Innovation\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nHemaSphere\\nGrants\\nTopics-in-Focus program\\n“We’ve always recognized the importance of exchanging research ideas. There is a lot of cross-country collaboration, both within Europe and more globally.”\\nDr Sue Pavord, President of the British Society for Hematology\\nOxford University Hospitals NIS FT, United Kingdom\\n“We’ve always recognized the importance of exchanging research ideas. There is a lot of cross-country collaboration, both within Europe and more globally.”\\nDr Sue Pavord, President of the British Society for Hematology\\nOxford University Hospitals NIS FT, United Kingdom\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-049ec083060697f21e9e4005\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4010, \"end\": 5610, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1600}], \"